<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" id="6e1c-15c5-ec26-3399" name="Homebrew - Leagues of Votann" revision="18" battleScribeVersion="2.03" library="false" gameSystemId="28d4-bd2e-4858-ece6" gameSystemRevision="130" type="catalogue" authorName="Isaac">
  <publications>
    <publication id="e1a3-795b-be05-784b" name="Leagues of Votann for The Horus Heresy 2.0 — Homebrew Conversion" shortName="HB - Leagues of Votann" />
  </publications>
  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Leagues of Votann" hidden="false" id="af4f-b87c-fd33-0f49" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="17ec-429b-92cd-9223" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="ccf7-97f6-5b38-8953" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grudgekeepers" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="d7ef-901b-fcf6-8dcc">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: During the enemy Shooting phase, a friendly Votann unit is selected as the target of a Shooting Attack. Effect: The targeted unit reacts. After the enemy Shooting Attack is fully resolved, the attacking unit gains 1 Judgement Token. The reacting unit may then make a Return Fire Shooting Attack against the attacking unit, following all standard rules for Return Fire. It can only do this if it has not been destroyed, is not Pinned, is not Falling Back, and the attacking unit is within Line of Sight and range of at least one of its weapons. Restriction: A unit that makes this Reaction cannot also make a Return Fire Reaction against the same Shooting Attack.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Debt Collector" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="f74b-6e9d-90ed-6096">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Any Phase Reaction). Trigger: During any phase of your opponent's turn, immediately after an enemy unit with at least 1 Judgement Token finishes resolving an action that has already triggered a friendly Votann unit's Reaction (such as Return Fire, Overwatch, or Interceptor), or immediately after an enemy unit with at least 1 Judgement Token declares a Charge or Shooting Attack against a friendly Votann unit that has already made a Reaction this phase. Effect: Remove 1 Judgement Token from the triggering enemy unit. At the cost of 1 point of your Reaction Allotment, one eligible friendly Votann unit may immediately make a Core Reaction (or Grudgekeepers) targeting that enemy unit. Restrictions: ; This reaction overrides the standard restriction that a single unit cannot make more than one Reaction per phase, allowing a unit that has already reacted this phase to react a second time against the marked target.; You may only use Debt Collector once per phase, and no single Votann unit may ever make more than two Reactions in the same phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Key Terms" id="ab51-c1ba-de9e-2937" hidden="false">
          <description>• Votann unit: any unit with the Eye of the Ancestors and League (X) special rules. Every unit in this document has both. Wherever these rules say "friendly Votann unit", they mean a friendly unit with those rules.
• Marked unit: an enemy unit with one or more Judgement Tokens.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="e90d-e5a8-f42d-da84" id="1ebc-4643-8ad5-6f4a" primary="true" name="Allegiance:" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="League" hidden="false" id="6fd5-ac50-fc3b-92fb">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="63aa-6c7c-4c34-9949" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="926e-0757-2ff1-99d1" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Greater Thurian League" hidden="false" id="53a0-2151-818f-1792" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Hold the Hold" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="37c5-9722-29cc-3135">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Assault phase). Trigger: An enemy unit declares a Charge against a friendly Greater Thurian League unit. Effect: The charged unit does not fire Overwatch. Instead, until the end of the Assault phase, every model in it gains +1 Attack and counts as having charged when determining the effects of Furious Charge (X).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Ancestral Bloodlines" id="a3e8-913e-3528-2f11" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with this special rule add +1 to their Leadership characteristic, to a maximum of 10.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Bastions of Grit" id="6a1b-2b9c-dcdf-e94c" hidden="false">
                  <description>An Infantry unit with this special rule that did not move during its most recent friendly Movement phase gains Feel No Pain (6+) until the start of its next Player Turn. For this rule, moving includes disembarking, but not Reaction moves made during the enemy turn. Sweeping Advance and Consolidation moves made after that Movement phase also cancel the bonus.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Kronus Hegemony" hidden="false" id="c420-ead6-6567-06b5" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Strike First" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="a9a4-15cb-e43a-6631">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Once per battle. Trigger: A friendly Kronus Hegemony unit is selected as the target of a Shooting Attack. Effect: The targeted unit immediately makes a Return Fire Shooting Attack against the attacking unit, before the attacking unit resolves its Shooting Attack. Remove casualties from this Reaction before the attacking unit makes its attacks.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Hegemony's Wrath" id="6d63-914b-01a8-917a" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units with this special rule add +1 to all Charge distance rolls.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Long Memory" id="f5d8-ca41-b23b-f268" hidden="false">
                  <description>If your Primary Detachment has the Kronus Hegemony special rule, you may select up to three enemy units during Marking the Grudge instead of two.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Trans-Hyperian Alliance" hidden="false" id="f1d3-30f8-4eba-00eb" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Rapid Redeployment" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="6fca-fb4a-96a3-b757">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Once per battle. Trigger: An enemy unit ends a Move or Rush within 12" of a friendly Trans-Hyperian Alliance Vehicle. A unit arriving from Reserves (including by Deep Strike or Outflank) does not trigger this Reaction. Effect: That Vehicle may immediately make a move of up to 6" in any direction. It cannot end this move within 1" of an enemy model, and it counts as having moved in its next Shooting phase.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Mechanised Kin" id="c83a-4599-1927-c9db" hidden="false">
                  <description>Vehicles with this special rule add +2 to their Movement characteristic.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Rapid Disembark" id="2779-9242-a533-344e" hidden="false">
                  <description>An Infantry unit with this special rule that disembarks from a Transport during the Movement phase may shoot in the following Shooting phase as though it had remained stationary.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Urani-Surtr Regulates" hidden="false" id="6323-25ed-9221-9ff4" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Ambush Fire" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="da7a-f813-24ae-91b0">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Trigger: An enemy unit ends a move within 12" of a friendly Urani-Surtr Regulates Infantry or Cavalry unit that is not Pinned, Falling Back or locked in combat. Effect: The reacting unit may immediately make a Shooting Attack against the triggering unit at its full Ballistic Skill. It must use Snap Shots if the target is a Flyer.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Pathfinders" id="9132-e36a-7f71-3a4a" hidden="false">
                  <description>Hernkyn units (such as Hernkyn Pioneers and Hernkyn Yaegirs) with this special rule gain the Outflank special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Precise Fire" id="1762-cbb6-8b68-611c" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units with this special rule may re-roll To Wound rolls of 1 when making Ranged attacks. Against a marked unit, they may instead re-roll all failed To Wound rolls with Ranged attacks.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Ymyr Conglomerate" hidden="false" id="a97e-906d-8554-dab7" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Emergency Shielding" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="a72a-056c-6a1b-7e32">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: A friendly Ymyr Conglomerate Vehicle is selected as the target of a Shooting Attack. Effect: Until that Shooting Attack ends, the targeted Vehicle has a 5+ Invulnerable Save against Glancing Hits, Penetrating Hits and hits from weapons with the Destroyer special rule inflicted by that attack.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Master Artisans" id="3fe9-860a-e963-51cc" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Battlesmith (X) special rule improve their Battlesmith target number by 1 (for example, 4+ becomes 3+).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Self-Repairing Hulls" id="0905-6b2a-d741-f294" hidden="false">
                  <description>At the end of each friendly Player Turn, roll a D6 for each Ymyr Conglomerate Vehicle on the battlefield that has lost Hull Points. On a 6, it regains 1 lost Hull Point, up to its starting value.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Rite of War" hidden="false" id="c60f-0f51-88e3-d6ea">
