    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="Kin Claim-Bastion" hidden="false" id="f1b0-63d2-e1bb-fb77" publicationId="e1a3-795b-be05-784b">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Void-Hardened Construction" id="2eb0-287f-345b-0253" hidden="false">
          <description>This Fortification has Armoured Ceramite: enemy weapons with the Melta special rule do not roll extra armour penetration dice against it</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Claim-Bastion Battlements" id="9267-bc3e-8ca0-8e28" hidden="false">
          <description>Counts as Open-Topped Battlements on the roof capable of holding up to 10 Infantry models, granting a 4+ Cover Save</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Ancestor's Claim" id="1113-df4f-40a8-ba14" hidden="false">
          <description>During deployment, if there is an Objective Marker wholly within your Deployment Zone, the Kin Claim-Bastion may be deployed within 1" of that Objective Marker. Friendly Legiones Votann units within 3" of it count as being within range of an Objective Marker controlled by their player for triggering rules and Warlord Traits, though the Claim-Bastion does not award Victory Points at the end of the battle</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Grudge-Ledger Array" id="b67d-4ef7-ada4-4745" hidden="false">
          <description>At the start of your Shooting phase, if a friendly Legiones Votann unit is embarked inside or occupying the battlements, select one visible enemy unit within 24" of the Kin Claim-Bastion; friendly Legiones Votann units within 12" of it treat that enemy unit as having +1 Judgement Token (to a maximum of 2) until the end of that Shooting phase</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Ironkin Cogitator-Targeting" id="5585-46a4-a0c4-6964" hidden="false">
          <description>During your Shooting phase, each hull-mounted weapon automatically fires at BS 3 at the nearest visible enemy unit within its 90° fire arc, and a roof-mounted turret at the nearest visible enemy unit within range (unless a model embarked inside or occupying the battlements fires it manually using its own Ballistic Skill)</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Note" id="a645-67c0-595e-9bef" hidden="false">
          <description>A heavy, prefabricated hexagonal redoubt anchored into bedrock by hydraulic pile-drivers, matching the resilience of an Imperial Bastion while housing Kin telemetry arrays.</description>
        </rule>
